 "system": {
  "description": {
   "value": "<p><em>Prerequisite: Must have Chemical Formulae</em></p>\n<p>You can choose to gain two of the following options (This feat can be taken more than once):<br />\n<strong>Transmute Explosion (3 CE)</strong>. As an action, you transmute the chemical composition of a 10 ft cube of air within 60 ft of you creating an explosion. All creatures within that cube must make a Constitution saving throw. On a failure, a creature takes 5d6 fire damage or half as much on a success. This becomes 8d6 at 11th level and 14d6 at 18th level.<br />\n<strong>Modify Attributes (2 CE)</strong>. As a bonus action, you swap your Strength, Dexterity, or Constitution scores for 1 minute (can end it as a free action).<br />\n<strong>Pressurization (3 CE)</strong>. As an action, you transmute the pressure of the air around you for up to 1 minute while concentrating. For the duration, you gain a 15 ft fly speed. This increases to 25 ft at 6th level, 40 ft at 11th level and 60 ft at 18th level.<br />\n<strong>Transmute Element (1 CE).</strong> When you deal a damage type from the following list, you can spend 1 CE to change that damage type to one of the other listed types: acid, cold, fire, lightning, poison, thunder.</p>",
   "chat": ""
  },
